## Why This Is Asked
Explores a new DP angle: subarray-level min as value, exact k non-overlapping blocks, with clear reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP with exact block count
- Precomputation of subarray minima
- Backtracking to obtain endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
// Assumes A is 1-indexed, n = A.length-1, k given
function maxSumMinSubarrays(A, n, k) {
  const M = Array.from({length: n+2}, ()=>Array(n+2).fill(0));
  for (let l=1; l<=n; l++) {
    let m = A[l];
    for (let r=l; r<=n; r++) {
      m = Math.min(m, A[r]);
      M[l][r] = m;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const opt = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) {
    for (let t=1; t<=k; t++) {
      for (let l=1; l<=i; l++) {
        const cand = dp[l-1][t-1] + M[l][i];
        if (cand > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = cand; opt[i][t] = l; }
      }
    }
  }
  // backtrack for endpoints
  let i = n, t = k, blocks = [];
  while (t > 0) {
    const l = opt[i][t];
    blocks.push([l, i]);
    i = l-1; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {sum: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a non-trivial partition DP with a non-linear subarray cost and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitions
- Range maximum queries (precomputation or on-the-fly)
- Path reconstruction via predecessor table

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  // precompute max for all ranges
  const mx = Array.from({length: n}, ()=> Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++){ mx[i][i]=A[i]; for(let j=i+1;j<n;j++) mx[i][j]=Math.max(mx[i][j-1], A[j]); }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(Infinity));
  const prv = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) dp[i][1] = mx[0][i-1]*(i);
  for(let j=2;j<=k;j++){
    for(let i=j;i<=n;i++){
      for(let t=j-1;t<=i-1;t++){
        const cost = dp[t][j-1] + mx[t][i-1]*(i-t);
        if(cost < dp[i][j]){ dp[i][j]=cost; prv[i][j]=t; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {cost: dp[n][k], cutPoints: []};
}
```

