## Why This Is Asked

This question tests deriving a solvable DP for contiguous partitions with a length-based cost, plus a linear-time optimization and path reconstruction.

## Key Concepts

- Contiguous partition DP
- Prefix sums and O(nk) optimization
- Backtracking to report segment endpoints

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxTotalWithCost(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const S = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) S[i] = S[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
    let bestVal = -Infinity, bestIdx = -1;
    for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
      const j = i - 1;
      if (dp[j][t-1] > -Infinity) {
        const cand = dp[j][t-1] - S[j] + c * j;
        if (cand > bestVal) { bestVal = cand; bestIdx = j; }
      }
      if (bestVal > -Infinity) {
        dp[i][t] = S[i] - c * i + c + bestVal;
        par[i][t] = bestIdx;
      }
    }
  }
  const segments = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  if (dp[n][k] <= -Infinity/2) return {best: -Infinity, segments: []};
  while (t > 0) {
    const j = par[i][t];
    segments.push([j+1, i]);
    i = j; t--;
  }
  segments.reverse();
  return {best: dp[n][k], segments};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt if c is paid only for non-first element or per segment boundary?
- How would you extend to maximize total value for at most k segments instead of exactly k?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to craft DP with a left-anchored subarray value and exact block counts, plus reconstruction for endpoints.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP with exactly k blocks
- Precomputation of bestStartAt[l][i]
- Reconstructing block boundaries via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeBestStartDP(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const bestStart = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(n).fill(-Infinity));
  for (let l=0; l<n; l++) {
    let best = -Infinity;
    for (let i=l; i<n; i++) {
      const sum = pref[i+1]-pref[l];
      best = Math.max(best, sum);
      bestStart[l][i] = best;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i=0; i<n; i++) dp[i][1] = bestStart[0][i];
  for (let t=2; t<=k; t++) {
    for (let i=t-1; i<n; i++) {
      let bestVal = -Infinity, bestL = -1;
      for (let l=t-1; l<=i; l++) {
        const prev = (l-1>=0) ? dp[l-1][t-1] : (t-1===0 ? 0 : -Infinity);
        const val = prev + bestStart[l][i];
        if (val > bestVal) { bestVal = val; bestL = l; }
      }
      dp[i][t] = bestVal;
      par[i][t] = bestL;
    }
  }
  return {dp, par};
}
